{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/136224-the-five-elemental-dragons-and-gaia","id":136224,"title":"The Five Elemental Dragons and Gaia","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-13T21:59:42-07:00","id":136224,"title":"The Five Elemental Dragons and Gaia","content":"The Five Elemental Dragons are actually gods, correct? But ones that help creation function? Or are they elementals? They're definitely not souls of Gaia, right? I recall something that only a jouten of Gaia's live in Yu-Shan while the rest of Gaia is exploring the Wyld.<br /> <br /> Also, is there any information of where Hesiesh and Pasiap sleep? And how they can be woken up? <br /> <br /> Just running a few Abyssals and thinking that making waking them up and watching destruction ensue, or killing the jouten of Gaia, might help Creation die some.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T22:21:37-07:00","id":136274,"title":"","content":"They're not Gods. They're not Elementals.<br /> They might be sub-souls of Gaia, or they might not be, I get the impression that different writers have had different opinions. I think the current consensus is they're not. They're just their own things, created by Gaia.<br /> <br /> I think Hesiesh and Pasiap sleep at (or under) the Elemental Poles of Fire and Earth respectively.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T22:36:24-07:00","id":136283,"title":"","content":"They're none of those, They're the Five Elemental Dragons, created by Gaia.<br /> <br /> Hesiesh and Pasiap sleep beneath the Elemental Poles of Fire and Earth.<br /> <br /> Killing Gaia's jouten will not have much of an effect on Creation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/393-godjaw","name":"Godjaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar393_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"665"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T22:55:55-07:00","id":136320,"title":"","content":"In First Edition it was never made clear what they were. In Second Edition it was strongly hinted that they were Gaia's 3rd Circle Souls. In Third Edition they are going to be something else - I believe they were called Gaia's Children.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T22:58:03-07:00","id":136322,"title":"","content":"I'll tell you what I told you on that thread on 4chan, anon. Creation is not Gaia, and vice versa. It's something that she created with another Primordial. The only sources that have ever tried to push a connection have had... issues with writers projecting personal points of view onto the setting, which didn't really mix well with it. Like the adventures in Exalted: the Autochthonians, for example. Those are not held up as bastions of reliable setting information, and nothing that agrees with them should be trusted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T23:02:15-07:00","id":136326,"title":"","content":"If you want to run a game where Gaia has a jouten and killing it kills Creation, or kills part of Creation, or where the Five Elemental Dragons are Gaia's souls, or are <i>not</i> Gaia's souls, or whatever, that is great. Go run that game! It sounds awesome!<br /> <br /> We're not going to nail it down so people can use it to win forum arguments, though. Or win arguments with their Storytellers. Or other players. Or so people feel constrained in what sorts of games they can consider running. As far as we're concerned, the Five Elemental Dragons are Gaia's children, and exploring what that means in an official or semi-official or whatever-sort-of-official-dev-statements-on-forums-count-as capacity is unnecessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 05-14-2014, 02:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":16}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-13T23:10:42-07:00","id":136339,"title":"","content":"The five elemental dragons are Gaia's kids. <a href=\"http://youtu.be/949eYdEz3Es\" target=\"_blank\">Here is a recreation of their birth</a>.<br /> <br /> They sleep in their beds, in Creation, where their element is strong. They find it comfy.<br /> <br /> They have places in Yu-Shan but they really don't like the atmosphere or the company.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Come and rock me Amadeus.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/296-hippokrene","name":"hippokrene","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar296_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2399"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T02:06:49-07:00","id":136410,"title":"","content":"The Five Elemental Dragons are actually Deathlord-made superweapons whose existence prior to the Great Contagion was falsely implanted in the minds of everyone by a Caine mind trick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T07:38:16-07:00","id":136695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/136224-the-five-elemental-dragons-and-gaia?p=136322#post136322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll tell you what I told you on that thread on 4chan, anon. Creation is not Gaia, and vice versa.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I agree. But then there are quotes such &quot;Without Mela, the air would grow stale&quot; and &quot;Mela and Daana\u2019d oversee all climate. The Dragon of Wood, Sextes Jylis, oversees growth. Together, these three Elemental Dragons permit mortal life&quot; from RoGD that at least hints at terrible destruction if one is killed. Maybe not the death of Creation, but something massive. (Unless waking up Hesiesh and Pasiap has the same effect as the Kukla, where his destruction makes land vital and despite the deaths caused, prevents shadowlands from forming.)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/136224-the-five-elemental-dragons-and-gaia?p=136326#post136326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as we're concerned, the Five Elemental Dragons are Gaia's children, and exploring what that means in an official or semi-official or whatever-sort-of-official-dev-statements-on-forums-count-as capacity is unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for that. I wasn't necessarily wanting a dev statement, I was only looking for some understanding. And even what you said helps.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T08:23:24-07:00","id":136763,"title":"","content":"the stuff you're referencing comes from second edition, DarkLord. I'm pretty sure the Kukla didn't re-fertilize the world in its original writeup, it was just the apocalyptic disaster in physical form that remained in the reserves of Heaven for whenever a mad and world-shattering dragon would be preferable to the unthinkable cataclysm that necessitated its release. Given the general disdain a lot of this community seems to possess for large swaths of the 2e run, I expect in Third it won't be engraved into canon that the Elemental Dragons' deaths would be obviously and immediately deleterious to the stability of Creation and survival of its inhabitants.<br /> <br /> That said, SLS is very right inasmuch as what works best for your game may not be what works best for all games, and vice versa. Wrestling with titanic, violent expressions of nature in order to cripple the world seems like a perfectly cool idea, and you should feel free to run with it.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, destroying a jouten, IIRC, results in the destruction of the whole Primordial; destroying the Emerald Mother would also shatter the world-comet Gnosis, and if the Dragons are her souls, one assumes that they too would be destroyed. If one subscribes to the idea that Gaia or the Dragons are tied to Creation's geomancy or Essence flows, it would probably also cripple many manses in the process. Then again, it's apparently possible for souls to survive the death of their greater part and be absorbed into other Primordials; one of the Voice of the Magnus segments implied this. Also, since Elementals do not spring from her directly, one can assume they would continue to exist. Make of that what you will.<br /> <br /> FWIW, I seem to recall the Elemental Dragons of Fire and Earth slumbering at their respective poles, but don't quote me on that. If nothing else, it's a reasonable place to start looking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":561,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","user":"Mockery","date":". 05-14-2014, 11:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T08:29:45-07:00","id":136768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/136224-the-five-elemental-dragons-and-gaia?p=136763#post136763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given the general disdain a lot of this community seems to possess for large swaths of the 2e run...</div> </div> </div> </div>Except that is all I have to go off, the 2nd edition stuff...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T08:48:18-07:00","id":136778,"title":"","content":"Assume more or less 2e cosmology is a blanks late beyond what's directly addressed in 3e. The editions between Exalted are going a tad bit for this Marval style Ultimate-Superior-Classic thing I think.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T09:09:14-07:00","id":136788,"title":"","content":"They <i>say</i> they're her Children, but that's just an indulgence of their pride; they're really just growths that budded off of Gaia and had independent life, as is the way of Primordials, who just happened to grow into heights of power to rival the Incarnae.<br /> <br /> Don't bring it up though, they get rather testy over it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>UKnown DarkLord</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then there are quotes such &quot;Without Mela, the air would grow stale&quot; and &quot;Mela and Daana\u2019d oversee all climate. The Dragon of Wood, Sextes Jylis, oversees growth. Together, these three Elemental Dragons permit mortal life&quot; from RoGD that at least hints at terrible destruction if one is killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lea once said that he wrote that stuff as a bit of damage control after another writer had referred to the Dragons in Compass: Wyld as doing stuff, in contravention of all other setting material that assumes their absence, and had given no thought to what that stuff actually was.<br /> <br /> Even the idea that Hesiesh and Pasiap are slumbering seems unnecessary; Pasiap can just be holding self-indulgent court upon or beneath the Omphalos.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T09:10:33-07:00","id":136790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/136224-the-five-elemental-dragons-and-gaia?p=136768#post136768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Except that is all I have to go off, the 2nd edition stuff...</div> </div> </div> </div>And that's very fair. I've said it once and I'll say it again: I'm waiting for distance to bring some element of 2e into focus and make us go, &quot;You know what? That was a really good idea there and we miss it.&quot;<br /> <br /> FWIW, I was there from the day the limited edition of the 1e core hit the shelves. This isn't boasting, it's a.) fact, and b.) something that I openly admit tends to skew my perspective when talking to other fans, since I forget that probably most people didn't get on that quickly, or may not even have seen anything from 1e at all.<br /> <br /> So there's the biases I'm immediately aware of. Take my posts with a grain of salt accordingly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T09:18:53-07:00","id":136794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/136224-the-five-elemental-dragons-and-gaia?p=136790#post136790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And that's very fair. I've said it once and I'll say it again: I'm waiting for distance to bring some element of 2e into focus and make us go, &quot;You know what? That was a really good idea there and we miss it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sure they're going to do something great with the Scarlet Dynasty one way or the other, but if there wasn't at least a reference to the goals and agendas of the Great Houses as set down in the Second Edition corebook, I'd definitely miss that. That whole section on the Realm, which does include some new details over the First Edition portrayal, was definitely top-notch to me (endorsement of the Empress and all).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T09:27:15-07:00","id":136800,"title":"","content":"On that note; what did 1st Edition say about the Five Elemental Dragons?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mockery</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/136224-the-five-elemental-dragons-and-gaia?p=136763#post136763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Also, destroying a jouten, IIRC, results in the destruction of the whole Primordial; destroying the Emerald Mother would also shatter the world-comet Gnosis, and if the Dragons are her souls, one assumes that they too would be destroyed. If one subscribes to the idea that Gaia or the Dragons are tied to Creation's geomancy or Essence flows, it would probably also cripple many manses in the process. Then again, it's apparently possible for souls to survive the death of their greater part and be absorbed into other Primordials; one of the Voice of the Magnus segments implied this. Also, since Elementals do not spring from her directly, one can assume they would continue to exist. Make of that what you will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, Gnosis is an extension of Gaia? I had the impression that it was some a planet sized artifact. Is it her world body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T09:35:10-07:00","id":136806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/136224-the-five-elemental-dragons-and-gaia?p=136800#post136800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On that note; what did 1st Edition say about the Five Elemental Dragons?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're supposed to reign over the Terrestrial gods, but have withdrawn into self-indulgence for most of the Second Age.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T09:35:19-07:00","id":136807,"title":"","content":"Bluuuuhhhh I'm supposed to be writing Tomb of Dreams right now why am I posting here?<br /> <br /> Okay. So! I wrote the Introduction and Chapters 1 and 3 of <i>The Roll of Glorious Divini(n)ty I</i>. I also developed the book, which means I oversaw the writing of chapters 2 and 4 and the appendix (I also wrote the bits in Chapter 4 that introduce the themes of each element, like the part about air elementals that starts &quot;Air elementals conceal an inner raging chaos beneath a veneer of cold order.&quot;) I was ultimately the one responsible for deciding what went into that book. So I'm largely responsible for the way the Five Elemental Dragons are portrayed there!<br /> <br /> I should share my thoughts.<br /> <br /> So, first of all, constraints shape creative expression. Late 1st edition &quot;revealed&quot; that the Five Elemental Dragons were the five souls of Gaia, or five <i>of</i> the souls of Gaia, or whatever. I say &quot;revealed&quot; in scare-quotes because up until that point, that had not been the intention. Once it was declared, though, there was no going back, so for the sake of consistency, the FEDs had to be presented in a manner consistent with being souls of Gaia thereafter. Also, the book <i>Compass of Celestial Directions, Volume II-The Wyld</i> talked about what the dragons were up to -- specifically the Dragons of Air, Water, and Wood were out and about doing things in Creation, and the Dragon of Fire was asleep at the Pole of Fire. It didn't mention what the Dragon of Earth was up to because it was a book about the Wyld, so the bits about the dragons went into the bits about the elemental poles and it didn't have a bit about the Pole of Earth.<br /> <br /> This, again, was a bit of a swerve, because up until that point, the FED had <i>never</i> been presented as &quot;Out and about, doing things.&quot; They were always written as being conspicuously absent from view. I actually contacted the author of Compass: Wyld to ask what was up with that, and the reply I got was &quot;I thought it would be neat if three of the dragons were out and about, governing spirit courts, fixing divine corruption, running oversight on the censors, bringing order to the world, etc..&quot; This made me facepalm, because that's never what they'd been written as up to before, and it sort of conflicted with the whole &quot;Nobody's at the wheel, divine corruption is rampant, even the censors are just assholes taking bribes to look the other way&quot; venue thing we have going that makes the setting so interesting for Solars who want to fix stuff.<br /> <br /> So I had to ask myself &quot;Okay, why are the dragons of Air, Water, and Wood out and about and <i>not</i> Fire? Also, what's up with the Dragon of Earth? And if three or four of the FEDs are out and about doing things, why hasn't anyone noticed? What could they be doing <i>other than</i> governing spirit courts, fixing divine corruption, running oversight on the censors, bringing order to the world, etc., because I sure don't want to write about them doing those things! And how can I write the FED in a manner that is <i>consistent</i> with being Gaia's souls without actually <i>saying</i> they are Gaia's souls (because I think coming out and saying it is sort of weaksauce)?&quot;<br /> <br /> After a lot of thought and stress and hair-pulling I decided on the solution I implemented: The Air, Water, and Wood Dragons are out and about <i>being the weather and ecosystem;</i> nobody sees them because they're integral to everything. And since everybody knows the far past was an age of earthquakes and volcanism and great geological upheavals and continents rearranging themselves and such, and the present doesn't have as much of that, I can say it's because the Earth and Fire Dragons are asleep and <i>not being</i> geological upheaval and volcanism, as opposed to the other three, who are awake and <i>are being</i> the atmosphere and the ocean currents and the ecosystem.<br /> <br /> As a solution it works. It's kinda neat! But as of 3rd Edition it's a solution to a problem we can fix at the root.<br /> <br /> For Third Edition you can pretty much expect us to throw out the idea that three of the FED are awake being the weather and ecosystem and that two are asleep, because we don't have a book saying &quot;The Air, Water, and Wood dragons are out and about doing stuff&quot; that we have to explain anymore. Likewise, we don't have to carefully allude to the idea that the FED are the souls of Gaia anymore, because we're just not going to establish it in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":229,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","user":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","date":". 05-14-2014, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":15}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T09:42:55-07:00","id":136813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/136224-the-five-elemental-dragons-and-gaia?p=136807#post136807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bluuuuhhhh I'm supposed to be writing Tomb of Dreams right now why am I posting here?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because you love us?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T09:44:54-07:00","id":136815,"title":"","content":"Personally, whether they're referred to much at all or not, I'd prefer an approach that plays up &quot;dragon&quot; more than &quot;elemental&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which is to say, while I'm okay with the idea of them having strong elemental associations, or power over the elements, I'd like a bit of a move away from the idea of them as a kind of elemental embodiment; that, first and foremost, they're a place to put some of the bigger cultural connotations of &quot;dragon&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T09:49:47-07:00","id":136819,"title":"","content":"I sort of think there are other places where those connotations can go.<br /> <br /> Like, I'm pretty fond of the idea that each of the Elemental Dragons is just massive in the amount of space it takes up, Godzilla-sized or bigger. Mountain-sized. And that precludes using them as actors in any conflict and pretty much relegates them to the role of <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Dumb_Object\" target=\"_blank\">Big Dumb Object</a>. Which I don't have a problem with! Better to have them big and impressive and ultimately sort of irrelevant than out and about setting cities on fire with their breath weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T09:51:01-07:00","id":136824,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/136224-the-five-elemental-dragons-and-gaia?p=136807#post136807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Third Edition you can pretty much expect us to throw out the idea that three of the FED are awake being the weather and ecosystem and that two are asleep, because we don't have a book saying &quot;The Air, Water, and Wood dragons are out and about doing stuff&quot; that we have to explain anymore. Likewise, we don't have to carefully allude to the idea that the FED are the souls of Gaia anymore, because we're just not going to establish it in the first place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will there be helps in 3rd edition to help Storytellers stat them up as 3rd circle souls, or greater elemental dragons or however the Storyteller decides to portray them?? Or will it just say they're there and leave what they do as a big blank slate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T09:58:52-07:00","id":136826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/136224-the-five-elemental-dragons-and-gaia?p=136824#post136824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Will there be helps in 3rd edition to help Storytellers stat them up as 3rd circle souls, or greater elemental dragons or however the Storyteller decides to portray them?? Or will it just say they're there and leave what they do as a big blank slate?</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect us to eventually get to the point where we're publishing guidelines for statting kaiju and Third Circle Souls, but I have no idea when and it doesn't seem to be in the early material queue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/229-stephen-lea-sheppard","name":"Stephen Lea Sheppard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar229_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T10:10:21-07:00","id":136838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/136224-the-five-elemental-dragons-and-gaia?p=136815#post136815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, whether they're referred to much at all or not, I'd prefer an approach that plays up &quot;dragon&quot; more than &quot;elemental&quot;.<br /> <br /> Which is to say, while I'm okay with the idea of them having strong elemental associations, or power over the elements, I'd like a bit of a move away from the idea of them as a kind of elemental embodiment; that, first and foremost, they're a place to put some of the bigger cultural connotations of &quot;dragon&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I alway saw things as the ultimate animal expressions fo the Five Elements you get fuckin' dragons. And that elementals become draconic because they are becoming more and more the platonic animal form related to that element, much like badgers are related to earth and phoenixes to fire.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T10:37:34-07:00","id":136871,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Hanged Man</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gnosis is Gnosis. We don't have a lot of details on it. An artifact would make sense. A Jouten, major Soul, Gaian Behemoth, or Weird Non-Sentient Charm Manifestation would also make sense. Or just a non-magical chunk of celestial material whose only unusual property is being the ride a Primordial zooms around the universe on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh! I could have sworn one of the writers claimed it was a world-jouten. Oh, well. Not relevant at this point, and with the lamentable gaps in the old forums archives it'd be difficult if not outright impossible to track down.<br /> <br /> (Further note: I've been into Exalted forever, but that doesn't mean I can't be flat-out wrong)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-14T14:24:55-07:00","id":137157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stephen Lea Sheppard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/136224-the-five-elemental-dragons-and-gaia?p=136819#post136819\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like, I'm pretty fond of the idea that each of the Elemental Dragons is just massive in the amount of space it takes up, Godzilla-sized or bigger. Mountain-sized.</div> </div> </div> </div>To clarify, when I say &quot;dragon&quot; I don't mean &quot;going around like Smaug&quot;, just... it's more in what they look like. Mostly to keep elemental embodiment ideas out of the Terrestrials.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, this is exactly what I see them as as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}